  "reason": "The records collectively identify the relevant FCC/B2 lamellar Al-Co-Cr-Fe-Ni alloy, show that pressure plus temperature can restructure HEAs, establish that coherent interfaces can transmit dislocations and relieve crack-producing stress concentrations, and associate multiple defect mechanisms with improved strength–ductility balance. However, none shows HPHT treatment of this Al0.7CoCrFeNi-type eutectic alloy producing a hierarchical coherent FCC/B2 pattern. The closest coherent-interface study uses a different refractory HEA and even limits applicability to brittle B2-containing systems, while pressure studies mainly concern FCC–HCP transformations in Cantor alloy. Thus the literature points toward the general strategy, but selecting hexahedron-anvil HPHT to create the specific coherent hierarchical architecture would still require a substantial new idea."
